 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The sounds that whistle",
   "texto": [
    "**Ж** sounds **zh**, like the French «j» of «je». **Ш** sounds **sh**. **Щ** is a **sh más larga y suave**, which we will write «sch». **Ч** sounds **ch**. **Ц** sounds **ts**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Vowels with «and»",
   "texto": [
    "**Я** sounds about **ya**, **Ю**, **yu**, and **Ё**, **yo**; the **ё** always bears the accent.",
    "**Е** can also start with a brief «and» sound: at the beginning of the word and after vowel, **ь** or **ъ** usually sound «ye»; after consonant, the vowel approaches «e» and softens that consonant.",
    "**Я**, **Ю** and **Ё** behave in a similar way: after a consonant (without a separator sign) they soften it; at the beginning or after vocal, **ь** or **ъ** add the «and» sound."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The weirdest letter",
   "texto": [
    "**Ы** does not exist in Spanish. It's a **i dicha con la lengua atrás**, as if your throat was squeezed when you said it. We will write it **y**: **ты** (you) = «ty», **мы** (we) = «my»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Two letters that don't sound",
   "texto": [
    "**Ь** has no sound of its own and usually indicates that the previous consonant is soft. **нь** sounds almost like «-»: **день** (day) = «day». After **ж, ш, ч, щ** does not change pronunciation: in **ночь**, for example, **ч** is already soft.",
    "**Ъ** is not pronounced. In prefix words, it separates the final consonant from the **е, ё, ю, я** prefix: the consonant is hard and a short «and» appears before the vocal, as in **подъезд** (entrance to a building)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The letter in the actual texts",
   "texto": [
    "**Ё** carries the accent and is pronounced «I». In student materials they are usually written with their two points; in many ordinary texts they are omitted and you will see **е** instead.",
    "Learn to recognize both forms: **ёлка / елка** (fir). The context helps to distinguish words like **всё** (all) and **все** (all)."
   ]
  },
